  "details": "I previously made a post that the camera grid overlay was off by a few pixels but it was since been marked as fixed. However after using the grid I still found that my photos and centering were off by a few pixels so I dug a little deeper.\n\nUpon testing, I found that the picture taken within the game and the picture produced was slightly different.\n\nThis is because the picture taken by the camera actually exceeds what is shown within the camera display by a few pixels. The display is actually cut off unevenly by the black border around the camera.\n\nPhoto 1 & 2 \n\nShows photo 1 of the camera display and the produced photo 2, the top and bottom of photo 2 exceeds the frame by about a pixel or two even though no space is shown on the camera display in photo 1\n\nPhoto 3 & 4\n\nThis time I tested the right and left parts of the display and found that the produced photo exceeds the frame on the left side by 3 or so pixels. \n\nThis is probably also the cause of why using the grid overlay to center the photo does not produce a photo that was completely centered because the display itself is off. Since the grid is probably bonded to the display it is also cut off unevenly by the black border.\n\nThank you for your attention and understanding, if you require any further evidence please a comment below.",
